{"text": "28 DORRANCE STREET, SUITE 400\n\neA AL ah om .\n\n401.891.7175 1\nAMERICAN CIVIL Li\nof RHODE ISLAND.\n\nDecember 15, 2016\n\n\u2018The Hon. Luis Aponte, President\nProvidence City Council\nty Hall\n25 Dorrance Street,\nProvidence, RI 02903\n\nDear Council Pre\n\nident Aponte:\n\nEarlier this week, the Providence Board of Contract and Supply recommended the\nexpenditure of hundreds of thousands of dollars for the purchase of body cameras for Providence\npolice officers. When this purchase request is brought before the City Couneil for consideration, we\nurge you and the rest of the Council to reject it unless and until the police department or the Council\nadopts strong standards in place for their use.\n\n\u2018The ACLU has had correspondence with the police department and various city officials on\nthis issue for well over a year. It has been our position that police body cameras have the ability to\nprovide a helpful layer of transparency and accountability in police-community relations ~ if proper\npolicies are in place, Unfortunately, they are not. The PD's current policy would allow the public to\nbe kept in the dark if a troubling incident of police misuse of force were to be captured on these\ncameras. The policy also, in our opinion, is not sufficiently precise in making sure that encounters\nwill be captured on tape from beginning to end. We question the expenditure of so much taxpayer\nmoney if, ultimately, the purchase is unlikely to promote trust in the community.\n\nT have enclosed for your review 2 copy of my most recent correspondence with Chief\n\u2018Clements about this matter. Whether adopted through language in the proposed Community Safety\nAct or as a separate ordinance or policy, we strongly encourage members of the Council to withhold\nsupport for the purchase of police body cameras until these critical issues of transparency and\naccountability are clearly, fully and properly addressed.\n\n\u2018Thank you in advance for considering our views.\n\nExecutive Director\nEnclosure\n\nce: Providence City Council\n\u2018The Hon. Jorge Elorza\nCommissioner Steven Pare\nCol. Hugh Clements, Jr.\nJeffrey Dana",
